        "root_concepts": "[family, demographic]",
        "section": "sociology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Family and Demographic Change",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "FIRST DEMOGRAPHIC TRANSITION (FDT) — 19th–20th century:\n  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n  Stage 1: High mortality + high fertility → stable (pre-industrial)\n  Stage 2: Mortality falls (sanitation, medicine) → population boom\n  Stage 3: Fertility falls (education, urbanization) → stable again\n  Stage 4: Low mortality + low fertility → below-replacement fertility"
    },
    {
      "id": "06-FAMILY-DEMOGRAPHIC-CHANGE.md#005",
      "path": [
        "06-FAMILY-DEMOGRAPHIC-CHANGE.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:sociology:06-family-demographic-change, git-history:sociology:06-family-demographic-change]",
        "canonical_path": "sociology/06-FAMILY-DEMOGRAPHIC-CHANGE.md",
