        "root_concepts": "[family, demographic]",
        "section": "sociology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Family and Demographic Change",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "FAMILY FORMS SPECTRUM:\n  Nuclear family    Two parents + children (biological or adopted)\n  Extended family   Three+ generations; lateral kin sharing household\n  Stem family       One child inherits; others move out (European peasant)\n  Polyandry         One woman, multiple husbands (rare — Tibetan fraternal)\n  Polygyny          One man, multiple wives (sub-Saharan Africa, parts of ME)\n  Single parent     One adult (divorce/death/never-married)\n  Cohabiting        Unmarried couple; with or without children\n  Same-sex family   All above structures, same-sex partners\n  Fictive kin       Non-biological social family networks (common in US Black communities)\n```"
    },
