      "text": "NUCLEAR FAMILY (husband-wife-children):\n  Idealized in 20th-century US as \"normal\" (breadwinner + housewife)\n  Historical context: became prevalent with industrialization\n    → Wage labor → adults move away from extended kin → nuclear household\n    → Pre-industrial: nuclear household embedded in larger household economy\n  \"Standard North American Family\" (Smith 1993) = ideological construct\n    → Most families always deviated: boarders, servants, grandparents, kin labor"
    }
